Diagnostics workflows:
Still rely on legacy compatibility paths
Expect these settings to exist even for workspace‑based AI
Do not gracefully fall back when they’re missing

APPINSIGHTS_INSTRUMENTATIONKEY: appInsights.properties.InstrumentationKey
APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_ROLE_NAME: functionAppName
WEBSITE_SITE_NAME: functionAppName

 
Your Function App is valid and runnable, but it is not “portal‑diagnostics complete”.
There are three concrete problems in the current templates that together explain exactly the behavior you’re seeing:
Application Insights is created as Workspace‑based with DisableLocalAuth = true, but the Function App is not linked in the way Diagnostics expects
Critical portal-injected app settings are missing
SCM / diagnostics assumptions are violated by Flex + private storage + no explicit diagnostics wiring
This combination causes:
✅ Deployments to work
✅ App runtime to work
✅ Log stream sometimes to work
❌ “Diagnose and solve problems” to fail with the generic portal error
1. Application Insights: this is the primary break
You create App Insights like this:
 
 
 
 
Bicep
 
resource appInsights 'Microsoft.Insights/components@2020-02-02' = {

  name: appInsightsName

  kind: 'web'

  properties: {

    Application_Type: 'web'

    WorkspaceResourceId: workspace.id

    DisableLocalAuth: true

  }

}


Show more lines
And you wire the Function App with:
 
 
 
 
Bicep
 
APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING: appInsightsConnectionString

APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_AUTHENTICATION_STRING: 'ClientId=${uamiClientId};Authorization=AAD'

Show more lines
Why this breaks Diagnose & Solve
Diagnose and Solve does NOT authenticate to App Insights using your Function App’s managed identity.
Internally, the diagnostics blade:
Queries App Insights via portal-owned first‑party identity
Expects local auth to be enabled, or at least classic compatibility metadata
Assumes the Function App is “AI‑linked” the same way portal creation does
When you set:
 
 
 
 
Bicep
 
DisableLocalAuth: true

Show more lines
you effectively block the diagnostics backend from querying telemetry, even though:
Your app can emit telemetry ✅
Application Insights exists ✅
The app runs ✅
This is a known but undocumented limitation of the diagnostics blade for Linux / Flex apps.
✅ What the portal does (that your template doesn’t)
Portal creation:
Leaves DisableLocalAuth = false
Adds both classic and workspace‑based metadata
Adds hidden tags linking the Function App and AI resource
✅ Minimum fix
Change App Insights to:
 
 
 
 
Bicep
 
properties: {

  Application_Type: 'web'

  WorkspaceResourceId: workspace.id

  DisableLocalAuth: false


Show more lines
You can still restrict access via RBAC — but diagnostics requires local auth enabled today.
2. Missing mandatory diagnostics app settings
You set:
 
 
 
 
Bicep
 
APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING

Show more lines
But you do NOT set:
 
 
 
 
Plain Text
 
APPINSIGHTS_INSTRUMENTATIONKEY

APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_ROLE_NAME

WEBSITE_SITE_NAME

 
Show more lines
Why this matters
Diagnostics workflows:
Still rely on legacy compatibility paths
Expect these settings to exist even for workspace‑based AI
Do not gracefully fall back when they’re missing
Portal creation always adds them. Bicep does not.
✅ Required additions
Add these to functionAppAppSettings:
 
 
 
 
Bicep
 
APPINSIGHTS_INSTRUMENTATIONKEY: appInsights.properties.InstrumentationKey

APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_ROLE_NAME: functionAppName

WEBSITE_SITE_NAME: functionAppName

Show more lines
Without these, diagnostics cannot correlate:
Resource → telemetry → health workflows
3. No diagnosticSettings resource (this matters more on Flex)
You do not define:
 
 
 
 
Bicep
 
Microsoft.Insights/diagnosticSettings


Show more lines
For Flex Consumption + Linux:
Portal auto‑creates diagnostic settings
IaC does not
Diagnostics blade expects logs/metrics to be queryable via LAW
Your App Insights exists, but platform logs are not wired.
✅ Required diagnostic settings
You should explicitly add:
 
 
 
 
Bicep
 
resource functionDiagnostics 'Microsoft.Insights/diagnosticSettings@2021-05-01-preview' = {

  name: 'functionapp-diagnostics'

  scope: functionApp

  properties: {

    workspaceId: workspace.id

    logs: [

      {

        category: 'FunctionAppLogs'

        enabled: true

      }

    ]

    metrics: [

      {

        category: 'AllMetrics'

        enabled: true

      }

    ]

  }

}

Show more lines
Without this:
The app works
The portal diagnostics backend has nothing to query
4. SCM assumptions + private storage (secondary but real)
This is not the main cause, but it contributes.
You have:
Private storage only
Managed identity–based deployment storage
Flex plan
No explicit SCM config
Diagnostics still calls SCM metadata endpoints, even on Flex.
You did not explicitly set:
 
 
 
 
Bicep
 
siteConfig: {

  scmType: 'None'

}

Show more lines
Portal-created Flex apps do.
This avoids diagnostics attempting unsupported SCM workflows.
Why manual portal-created apps work
Portal creation silently does all of the following:
Enables local auth on App Insights
Adds legacy AI settings
Adds diagnosticSettings
Adds hidden tags and metadata
Shapes siteConfig for diagnostics compatibility
Your Bicep is correct, but too strict for today’s diagnostics tooling.
Final verdict (support-safe, precise)
✅ Your architecture is valid

✅ Your security posture is intentional

✅ Your suspicion was correct
❌ Azure “Diagnose and solve problems” does not support:
DisableLocalAuth = true on App Insights
Missing legacy AI settings
No diagnosticSettings
Flex + private storage without portal metadata
 
 
 